---Emitted when an outcome evaluation cycle completes. Carries the verdict and aggregate token usage. A verdict of `needs_revision` means another evaluation cycle follows; `satisfied`, `max_iterations_reached`, `failed`, or `interrupted` are terminal — no further evaluation cycles follow.
---@class anthropic.beta_sessions.BetaManagedAgentsSpanOutcomeEvaluationEndEvent
---@field type string
---@field id string Unique identifier for this event.
---@field processed_at string Timestamp when outcome evaluation ended.
---@field outcome_evaluation_start_id string The id of the corresponding `span.outcome_evaluation_start` event.
---@field iteration number 0-indexed revision cycle, matching the corresponding `span.outcome_evaluation_start`.
---@field result string Evaluation verdict. 'satisfied': criteria met, session goes idle. 'needs_revision': criteria not met, another revision cycle follows. 'max_iterations_reached': evaluation budget exhausted with criteria still unmet — one final acknowledgment turn follows before the session goes idle, but no further evaluation runs. 'failed': grader determined the rubric does not apply to the deliverables. 'interrupted': user sent an interrupt while evaluation was in progress.
---@field explanation string Human-readable explanation of the verdict. For `needs_revision`, describes which criteria failed and why.
---@field usage anthropic.beta_sessions.BetaManagedAgentsSpanModelUsage Aggregate token usage for this evaluation cycle. Sums across all grader model requests within the cycle.
---@field outcome_id string The `outc_` ID of the outcome being evaluated.

